# Build context filter for the two images: infra/Dockerfile and infra/stream/Dockerfile.
#
# Both Dockerfiles COPY a known, small set - src/music.ts, src/sound.ts, plugins/, and
# infra/{sounds,music,models,stream,entrypoint.sh,server.cfg,plugins.ini,build-hlds.sh,
# build-plugin.sh}. Everything listed below is either not read by any stage or must not leave the
# host at all, and together they were ~180 MB of the context on every build.
#
# The list is deliberately short: a pattern here that matches a COPY source breaks the build with a
# "not found" that says nothing about the cause, so nothing under src/, plugins/, infra/ or config/
# is filtered.

# History and VCS metadata: never needed, and .git alone is ~10 MB.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets. .env is not COPYed by any stage, but it is the one file that must not be handed to the
# Docker daemon in the first place: it holds the RCON password, the panel token and the stream key.
.env
.env.*

# The cheap-mode runtime state: the panel's SQLite database, the OAuth token file and the override.
data

# Build and test output: out/ is ~130 MB of renders and recordings, node_modules/ ~32 MB.
out
node_modules
.tmp-*

# Local scratch: build logs at the repository root, and the operator's own capture files.
*.log
logs

# Material that only developers read. The API and the encoder run from this repository mounted into
# the container, not from the image, so none of it is needed at build time.
docs
test
scripts
assets
overlay
public
